+
+## Payload gate update — second PROPER-FIX checkpoint
+
+Hypothesis: inherited m681 calibration and embedded firmware remain wrong even
+once U10 GPIO and power wiring is corrected. FACT: own stock `gtp_init_panel`
+ffffffc000816d78 copies one 186-byte group at ffffffc000c005f8; groups1..5 are
+empty, and the own probe calls no m681 cover-configuration path. Its dimensions
+are 720x1280. Donor group0 is 1080x1920 and has different bytes. Own config SHA256
+`5b18a65bd909dfba3eab28e3a0c888f39cb78c82c7c97470f839e9b7f8afcfe1`;
+version0x4c, checksum8=0, fresh flag1. Own code retains the config's dimensions
+rather than applying the donor GTP_CUSTOM_CFG override.
+
+FACT: U10 `gup_init_update_proc` ffffffc00081bdc8 starts
+`gup_update_proc(NULL)`; that function ffffffc000819ee0 reads embedded firmware
+at ffffffc0010e8a88: 14-byte header plus 0x16000 data bytes. Total90126,
+SHA256 `52eb3e6d0985c4568677833d7bd09580d276650832e65bee064ec8196667f1f2`,
+PID915L, VID header bytes3007, big-endian data-word sum16=0. The donor header
+contains90126 different bytes (SHA256
+`fd9a82fe019316a5d1e9d387730cc8976118b7a42c38f8c65c6ea6e388e88c4a`).
+
+Evidence: private receipts `u10-cfg-gtp-init-panel-mcp.json`,
+`u10-cfg-gup-update-proc-mcp.json`, `u10-cfg-gup-init-update-proc-mcp.json`,
+`u10-cfg-config-read-memory-mcp.json`,
+`u10-cfg-firmware-read-memory-mcp.json`, all under the durable private directory
+above. Full MCP reads of both payloads match their raw-kernel slices exactly.
+No payload bytes or reconstructed firmware are committed or redistributed.
+
+Files/why: GT9XX_MZ Makefile requires both privately generated headers via
+`GT9XX_U10_PRIVATE_INCLUDE` for U10 and fails if absent. The custom header
+selects the private config and excludes the donor config pool; own U10 uses
+config dimensions and omits the unsupported donor cover-table callback.
+The updater selects the private firmware header with no donor fallback.
+Kconfig also pins MT6755 and the MT6353 new-architecture PMIC owner.
+
+Generation and checks from the fleet export directory:
+`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 tools/extract_u10_goodix_private.py`
+`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 tools/validate_u10_profile.py kernel-checkout`
+
+FACT: extractor verifies kernel SHA, full MCP byte equality, both payload
+SHAs/checksums and config dimensions before emitting private headers. Existing
+private output may only be reused byte-for-byte. Preprocessing verifies exact
+selected config/FW array hashes, absence of donor dimensions/cover callback,
+and unchanged default driver/updater tokens. Makefile dry parsing fails on
+missing private path/header and passes with validated private inputs. These
+checks do not compile or run kernel code.
+
+Expected next marker: after own DT and remaining callback gates, a source build
+must select the exact private CFG/FW hashes above; a later authorized runtime
+capture should show own GT915L/config identity and720x1280 coordinates. Rollback
+if either source selection uses donor bytes, raw/MCP identity differs, or the
+legacy profile changes. The private firmware is controller data referenced by
+custom source, not a stock kernel/prebuilt image.
+
+Remaining gates: no own U10 DTS/DCT/build selection yet; FT/Goodix coexistence,
+MT6353 rail registration, source firmware-update policy/algorithm equivalence,
+gesture/suspend callbacks and all non-touch drivers still require validation.
+The source profile remains default off and no defconfig enables it. Earlier
+paragraphs listing unresolved CFG/FW *addresses and bytes* are superseded by
+this update; they do not imply that the complete driver or board now works.
